      "content": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Many studies have found a positive association between levels of dissolved organic carbon and\nmercury in bodies of fresh water undisturbed by human activity. Stéphane Guédron, Delphine\nTisserand, and colleagues did not find this correlation in an examination of freshwater bodies\nimpacted by wastewater, but Michael E. Berndt and Travis K. Bavin, who studied freshwater\nbodies disturbed by mining, did find it, leading some scientists to hypothesize that wastewater\naffects water chemistry differently than mining does. Guédron, Tisserand, and colleagues’ study,\nhowever, was conducted in Laos, whereas Berndt and Bavin’s study was conducted in the United\nStates, suggesting that \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_"
        }
      ],
      "prompt": [
        {
