      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "the discrepancy in the two studies’ results may be attributable to underlying environmental\ndifferences rather than the effects of wastewater and mining."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "levels of dissolved organic carbon and mercury are both much higher in bodies of fresh water\nimpacted by wastewater than they are in bodies of fresh water disturbed by mining."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "disturbances related to wastewater likely affect significantly more bodies of fresh water than\ndisturbances related to mining do."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "bodies of fresh water impacted by wastewater are more common in Laos than in the United\nStates."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
